{
 "id": "016-kucuk-yara-buyuk-yardim",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "Little Graze, Big Help",
 "theme": "Asking for help and first aid after an accident",
 "blurb": "Deniz falls while running in the park and scrapes her knee. Her friend Ali knows what to do: he doesn't touch the graze, he tells the teacher, and he fetches the first-aid kit.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "ali": "Ali",
  "deniz": "Deniz",
  "ogretmen": "Miss Nur"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "In autumn, Miss Nur's class came to the park. Rustle rustle went the leaves! Deniz and Ali played tag. “Catch me, Ali!” Deniz ran like the wind. Whoosh!",
   "hits": {
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Catch me, Ali!"
    },
    "ali": {
     "say": "I'm coming, I'm coming!"
    },
    "ogretmen": {
     "say": "What a lovely game you're playing!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Deniz!",
   "ask": "What game do you like playing most in the park?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 9,
     "fx": "yaprak"
    },
    {
     "w": 26,
     "fx": "ruzgar"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Suddenly Deniz's foot caught on a stone. Thud! Deniz fell to the ground. Her knee was scraped, and it stung and stung. Deniz was very frightened. Her heart went thump, thump. “Oww, my knee!”",
   "hits": {
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Oww, my knee hurts!"
    },
    "ali": {
     "say": "Deniz! Are you all right?"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the stone!",
   "ask": "How is Deniz feeling now? Have you ever fallen over? What did you feel?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 29,
     "fx": "kalp"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Ali came to Deniz straight away. “I'm here, I'm right beside you,” he said. Deniz whispered: “Can you clean it?” Ali shook his head. “No, grown-ups clean grazes. I'll…” Then he thought, and thought…",
   "hits": {
    "ali": {
     "say": "I'm here, right beside you!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Can you clean it?"
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Ali will do?",
    "res": "Both are safe ways! Let's see.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "He runs to the teacher"
     },
     {
      "l": "He calls out to her"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ali!",
   "ask": "Why didn't Ali touch the graze? What do you think he should do now?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Ali ran to Miss Nur. Tap tap tap! “Miss Nur, Deniz fell over! She scraped her knee.” Miss Nur was sitting down; she got up at once: “Thank you, Ali! I'll go to Deniz. Can you fetch the first-aid kit?”",
   "hits": {
    "ogretmen": {
     "say": "Thank you, Ali! Can you fetch the kit?"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Oww… come quick, Ali!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "say": "Tap tap tap!",
    "done": "Ali told the teacher!",
    "msg": "You told a grown-up!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch Ali so he runs!",
   "ask": "What did Ali tell the teacher? What would you say?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Miss Nur sat down beside Deniz. She washed the graze with clean water. Splish splash! The water stung a little. Deniz breathed in deep through her nose and let it out slowly through her mouth. Ffff… Ahh! Then Miss Nur dried it with a clean cloth. Pat pat! Last of all, she took a heart plaster out of the kit and stuck it on.",
   "hits": {
    "ali": {
     "say": "Here's the kit, Miss Nur!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Ffff… The water stung a bit, but it's gone now."
    },
    "ogretmen": {
     "say": "You breathed beautifully, Deniz."
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Washed, dried, plaster on. All done!",
    "msg": "You did it in order!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch the water first!",
   "ask": "What did Miss Nur do, in order, while she cleaned the graze?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 13,
     "fx": "musluk"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Deniz looked at her knee. A heart plaster! “My knee is all dressed up!” she laughed. “What if it was a big accident?” asked Ali. Miss Nur explained calmly: “Then grown-ups call 112. Help comes straight away.” Deniz hugged Ali: “Thank you, Ali!” The graze was small, but the help was great big!",
   "hits": {
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Thank you, Ali! My knee is all dressed up!"
    },
    "ali": {
     "say": "What if it was a big accident?"
    },
    "ogretmen": {
     "say": "Then grown-ups call 112."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the teacher!",
   "ask": "What do grown-ups do if there's a big accident? Who do you run to after a little accident, and what do you say to them?"
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "HSAB.11 Protecting themselves in situations of danger and accidents: knows what to do when an accident happens; does not touch the graze themselves and tells a trusted grown-up straight away. Knows the emergency numbers: says that in a big accident, grown-ups call 112.",
   "TADB.3 Analysing what they hear: identifies the parts of the events in the story and retells them in the order they happened (fell → told a grown-up → graze washed and dried → plaster put on).",
   "E2.1 Empathy and SDB2.3 Social Awareness: notices the fear and pain of a friend who has fallen; says supportive words such as “I'm here, I'm right beside you.”",
   "D20 Helpfulness: chooses safe ways to help a friend who needs it (telling a grown-up, fetching the kit, staying beside them). D13 Healthy Living: knows that a graze is washed with clean water and covered with a plaster."
  ],
  "once": [
   "Point to the children on the cover: “These are Deniz and Ali. What do you think they're playing in the park?”",
   "Link it to Red Crescent Week (29 October–4 November): “What does helping mean? Who have you helped, and how?”",
   "Show the class first-aid kit, closed: “What might be inside this kit? Who uses it?”"
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "Stop on page 2: “Deniz's heart is going thump, thump. What happens in your body when you're frightened?”",
   "On page 3, after the prediction is chosen, ask: “Why didn't Ali touch the graze?” (Grown-ups clean grazes.)",
   "On page 5, say the order out loud: “First water, then cloth, last of all plaster.” Breathe like Deniz: in deep through the nose, out slowly through the mouth."
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "Have the child tell the events in order: “What happened first? Then what did Ali do? What happened last?”",
   "Have each child say who they would tell if there was a little accident in the classroom or the garden (the teacher, the assistant teacher, a member of school staff).",
   "Say 112 together with a rhythm (“one-one-two”) and add: “Grown-ups call this number in a big accident; it is never called for a joke.”",
   "What do we look out for when running in the park? (looking ahead, slowing down on stony or wet ground, tying shoelaces) Draw safe running rules for the park together."
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "Little Helpers First-Aid Game",
   "sure": "20 min",
   "materyal": "The class first-aid kit (only the teacher opens it), a doll, colourful plaster stickers, four picture event cards (falling, telling a grown-up, washing, plaster), a bottle of water, a clean cloth",
   "adim": [
    "The teacher opens the kit, shows and names the items one by one; the children only look.",
    "Role play: the doll “falls over.” One child stays beside it and says “I'm here, I'm right beside you.”, one child tells the teacher, one child brings the closed kit. The teacher first washes their hands or puts on gloves, then shows the cleaning steps: first water, then cloth, last of all plaster.",
    "The children put the picture event cards in the order they happened and tell the story in their own words.",
    "To close, each child sticks a colourful plaster sticker on a friend's arm and says a helping sentence (first asking permission: “May I stick it on?”)."
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "How did Deniz feel when she fell? How did Ali comfort her?",
   "Who do you tell at home if there's a little accident? Who at school?",
   "Which number do grown-ups call in a big accident?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Our Family Help Corner",
   "d": "Find the first-aid box at home together; you show the items while your child only looks and says their names. Then, on a piece of paper, draw with your child the grown-ups they can ask for help at home, write 112 in big numbers in the corner and hang it on the fridge. Remind them: “Grown-ups call this number in a big accident; it is never called for a joke.”"
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read “Little Graze, Big Help.” When Deniz falls and scrapes her knee in the park, her friend Ali helps her: he doesn't touch the graze, he tells the teacher and fetches the first-aid kit; the teacher cleans the graze. At home too, you can talk about telling a grown-up first after a little accident, and about grown-ups being the ones who clean a graze; the adult washes their hands first. Remember together that in a big accident grown-ups call 112, and that this number is never called for a joke."
 },
